#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Dustwater: a third game for the Blobber engine, after the rules of
Mutant Future.

A hundred and some years after the bombs, the village of Dustwater lives
on what its old purifier can pull out of one bitter well.  The purifier
is failing: its filter core is clogged, its fusion cell nearly flat.  A
band of the village's misfits (pure humans, mutants, a plant and an
android) go out into the wastes to find replacements: a filter core in
the waterworks under the ruins of Carvel, and a fusion cell in the
sealed military bunker the old maps call Facility Nine.

The rules follow Mutant Future: hit points rolled as dice equal to
Constitution, the Mutant Future ability bonuses and saving throws, no
classes (each character's role is only what they're good at), levels
that bring a random gain rather than more hit points, mutations that
work as powers or passive traits, and radiation that can give a mutant a
new one.

Run it with ./dustwater (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.dustwater.json.  ./dustwater --selftest checks the maps, and
--balance plays its fights with a simulated player.
"""

